  <title>Units</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Edit</gui><gui>Units</gui></guiseq>, or <gui>Unit</gui> on a
  product, lists the units products can be sold in: each, foot, pound,
  box. Changes are saved as you make them.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Click <gui>New</gui> and type the <gui>Name</gui>, and an
    <gui>Abbr</gui> to print on invoices if you like.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose or type its <gui>Category</gui>, what it measures, such as
    length or weight.</p></item>
    <item><p>To record how it relates to a smaller unit, choose that unit in
    <gui>Of unit</gui> and type how many in <gui>Equals</gui>: a yard equals 3
    of foot.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>The list keeps each category together, smallest unit first, worked out
  from what each unit equals. A unit cannot be measured in itself, or in a
  unit that is already measured in it.</p>

  <p>Check <gui>Standard</gui> on the unit new products start with. Only one
  unit is the standard.</p>

  <section id="delete">
  <title>Deleting a unit</title>
  <p><gui>Delete</gui> removes the selected unit. It is refused for the
  standard unit, and for a unit another one is measured in. If products use
  the unit, you are asked whether to move them to another unit first: choose
  it and click <gui>Update and Delete</gui>.</p>
  </section>

